{title: How Firm a Foundation}
{artist: John Rippon’s Selection / Joseph Funk}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 2/2}
{score: how-firm-a-foundation.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (How_Firm_A_Foundation-Foundation-Protection) and the Cyber Hymnal score (82% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]How firm [C]a foun[G]dation, ye saints of the [D7]Lord,
[D7]Is [G]laid [C]for your [G]faith in His [D7]excellent [G]Word!
[G]What more can He [Em]say [Bm]than to [G]you He hath [D7]said,
[D7]You, [G]who [C]unto [G]Jesus for [D7]refuge have [G]fled?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]In ev[C]ery con[G]dition, in sickness, in [D7]health;
[D7]In [G]po[C]verty's [G]vale, or a[D7]bounding in [G]wealth;
[G]At home and a[Em]broad, [Bm]on the [G]land, on the [D7]sea,
[D7]As [G]thy [C]days de[G]mand, shall thy [D7]strength ever [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Fear not, [C]I am [G]with thee, O be not dis[D7]mayed,
[D7]For [G]I [C]am thy [G]God and will [D7]still give thee [G]aid;
[G]I’ll strengthen and [Em]help [Bm]thee, and [G]cause thee to [D7]stand
[D7]Up[G]held [C]by My [G]righteous, om[D7]nipotent [G]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]When through [C]the deep [G]waters I call thee to [D7]go,
[D7]The [G]ri[C]vers of [G]woe shall not [D7]thee over[G]flow;
[G]For I will be [Em]with [Bm]thee, thy [G]troubles to [D7]bless,
[D7]And [G]sanc[C]tify [G]to thee thy [D7]deepest dis[G]tress.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]When through [C]fiery [G]trials thy pathways shall [D7]lie,
[D7]My [G]grace, [C]all su[G]fficient, shall [D7]be thy sup[G]ply;
[G]The flame shall not [Em]hurt [Bm]thee; I [G]only de[D7]sign
[D7]Thy [G]dross [C]to con[G]sume, and thy [D7]gold to re[G]fine.
{end_of_verse}
